ng, we IMHO should provide such behavior by default (if no `-r` given).  Otherwise it is not clear what would be the role of `-r` in this case -- just to traverse the entire tree regardless either it is specified or not?  IMHO renders `diff` unusable in any reasonably \"rich\" hierarchy.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578589979,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzNTE5MDUzOQ=="},"target":"6ff2cfd38364d2b60f051ea4f6a676c1e741d59ddec2499f394d8061fba92eb6","message":"`git status` and `git diff` have at least an explicit `--ignore-submodules=dirty`. We don't have anything like that conveniently exposed and with `-r` semantic we are adding, we IMHO should provide such behavior by default (if no `-r` given).  Otherwise it is not clear what would be the role of `-r` in this case -- just to traverse the entire tree regardless either it is specified or not?  Current behavior simply renders `diff` unusable in any reasonably \"rich\" hierarchy for comparing against working tree of current dataset.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578590068,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjY2MTc0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3990#issuecomment-572661745"},"message":"may be at least \n```\n  -e {no|commit|full}, --eval-subdataset-state {no|commit|full}\n                        Evaluation of subdataset state (clean vs. modified)\n                        can be expensive for deep dataset hierarchies as\n...\n```\nof `datalad status` should then be exposed in `diff` as well.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578590778,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjY2NjI3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3990#issuecomment-572666277"},"message":"FTR, for my own understanding of effect of `-r` for `diff` ATM.  With o